---
/**
 * The reason behind a feature, as the book prints it: `<Why>one or two sentences</Why>`.
 * Every feature on these pages is said once, then its reason in one of these.
 * The markdown copy renders it as "**Why:** …" (src/lib/markdown-partials.ts).
 */
---

<div class="qwhy"><span class="qwhy-label">Why</span><div class="qwhy-text"><slot /></div></div>

<style>
  .qwhy {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    margin: 1rem 0 1.25rem;
    padding: 0.125rem 0 0.125rem 0.875rem;
    border-left: 2px solid #fcc620;
  }
  .qwhy-label {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #b07d00;
  }
  :global(:root[data-mode="dark"]) .qwhy-label {
    color: #fcc620;
  }
  .qwhy-text {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--nb-foreground);
  }
  .qwhy-text :global(p) {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .qwhy-text :global(p + p) {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
